>> title: Sesame Balls
>> category: Dumplings & Rolls
>> tags: glutinous rice, red bean, chinese, deep-fry, sweet
>> counters: Dim Sum Counter
>> aka: jin deui, jian dui, zin deoi, 煎堆, sesame ball, deep fried sesame ball, matuan
>> pairs-with: red-bean-paste
>> servings: 12
>> time: 1 hr 30 min
>> slack: unforgiving — a fryer run hot puffs the shell before the middle cooks and it bursts, which is boiling oil moving quickly
>> step.1: stir the sugar into hot water, cool 10 min
>> step.2: knead to a soft dough, rest 20 min
>> step.3: seal the paste inside 12 balls
>> step.4: roll them damp, then through the sesame
>> step.5: fry 300°F (150°C) 12 min, pressing them under

Stir @brown sugar{1/3%cup}(70 g) into @hot water{2/3%cup}(160 mL) until it has dissolved, then ~cool{10%min} to blood warm.

Knead @glutinous rice flour{2%cups}(280 g) and @wheat starch{2%Tbs}(20 g) into @&(~1)sugar syrup{} to a dough that takes a thumbprint without cracking, then ~rest{20%min}.

Divide @&(~1)dough{} into 12 and seal @red bean paste{1%cup}(280 g; rolled into 12 balls) inside each one, working the seam closed so no air is shut in with it — a trapped bubble bursts the ball in the oil.

Roll @&(~1)balls{} under a damp palm and then through @white sesame seeds{3/4%cup}(100 g), pressing hard enough that the seeds bed in.

Fry @&(~1)balls{} in @peanut oil{6%cups}(1.4 L; started at 300°F/150°C) for ~fry{12%min}, turning them and pressing them gently against the side of the #pot{} as they rise, until they have tripled and gone hollow.
